WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.240
A liquid-cooled rack can still reject substantial heat to air.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.360
Components outside the liquid-cooled path, power conversion and other equipment may depend

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:08.940
on airflow.

4
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.080
Determine the actual heat split from the selected equipment and operating conditions;

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.400
don't assume a universal percentage.

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.440
Follow the air from its intended inlet to its outlet.

7
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.980
Blanking and containment can prevent bypass or recirculation, but only if the

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.400
installed configuration preserves those boundaries.

9
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.300
Cable bundles, accessories and temporary service arrangements can obstruct the path or

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.580
open unintended gaps.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.120
Review normal operation and the allowed degraded conditions.

12
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.340
A cooling proposal must state what remains supported if a fan, liquid

13
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.560
path or receiving system changes state.

14
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.660
Neither a liquid connection nor a rack-level heat rating proves that each

15
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.400
component remains within its limits.

16
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.400
Ask for the equipment heat-rejection requirements and the site's commitment at the

17
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.160
relevant boundary.

18
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.880
The aim is a complete thermal path, including the air-side remainder, rather

19
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.580
than a liquid-only diagram that leaves some heat with nowhere demonstrated to

20
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:00.840
go.

